        "content": "<p>epitaphial opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15295\">issue #15295</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>wasi-preview1-component-adapter: nonblocking regular-file read returns EAGAIN before host I/O completes</h1>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>A regular file opened with O_RDWR|O_NONBLOCK immediately returns EAGAIN on its first read. The file position therefore remains zero, and a subsequent write overwrites the first byte. Direct P1 reads 'a' and writes at offset 1.</p>\n<p>Confirmed with the standalone C program below, without any custom test driver or trace format. Each lane reproduced the same output 5/5 times in fresh directories on Wasmtime 46.0.0 (Release and Debug), 47.0.2, and 50.0.1. Wasmtime 50.0.1 was the latest upstream release at verification time.</p>\n<h2>Minimal reproducer (<code>repro.c</code>)</h2>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"C\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;errno.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;fcntl.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;unistd.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">show_file</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">17</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_RDONLY</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">ssize_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">read</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file: rv=%zd content=%s</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">byte</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_CREAT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_TRUNC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_WRONLY</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mo\">0644</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"abcdefghijklmnop\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_RDWR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_NONBLOCK</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">ssize_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">read_rv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">read</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"kt\">byte</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"read: rv=%zd errno=%d (%s) byte=%c</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">read_rv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"n\">strerror</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">read_rv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">byte</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'?'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">ssize_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">write_rv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"write: rv=%zd errno=%d (%s)</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">write_rv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">strerror</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">show_file</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Exact commands</h2>\n<p>Run in a new empty directory. The first command downloads the official v50.0.1 command adapter; <code>clang</code>, <code>wasm-tools</code>, and <code>wasmtime</code> must be on the stated paths or adjusted to local installations.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-fLO<span class=\"w\"> </span>https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/releases/download/v50.0.1/wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm\n/opt/wasi-sdk/bin/clang<span class=\"w\"> </span>--target<span class=\"o\">=</span>wasm32-wasip1<span class=\"w\"> </span>-std<span class=\"o\">=</span>c17<span class=\"w\"> </span>-O2<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Wall<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Wextra<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Werror<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_rc_nb_read_eagain.c<span class=\"w\"> </span>-o<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm\nwasm-tools<span class=\"w\"> </span>component<span class=\"w\"> </span>new<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm<span class=\"w\"> </span>--adapt<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">wasi_snapshot_preview1</span><span class=\"o\">=</span>wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm<span class=\"w\"> </span>-o<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_adapter.wasm\nwasmtime<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm<span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>wasmtime<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_adapter.wasm\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Expected vs. actual output (Wasmtime 50.0.1)</h2>\n<p><strong>Direct P1 (expected):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>read: rv=1 errno=0 (Success) byte=a\nwrite: rv=1 errno=0 (Success)\nfile: rv=16 content=aAcdefghijklmnop\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><strong>Adapter P2 (actual):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>read: rv=-1 errno=6 (Resource temporarily unavailable) byte=?\nwrite: rv=1 errno=0 (Success)\nfile: rv=16 content=Abcdefghijklmnop\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Root cause</h2>\n<p>A host <code>FileInputStream</code> starts in <code>ReadState::Idle</code>. Its nonblocking <code>read</code> starts a blocking task and immediately returns empty <code>Bytes</code>; <code>Waiting</code> also returns empty <code>Bytes</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi/src/p2/filesystem.rs#L116-L139\"><code>filesystem.rs:116-139</code></a>). The adapter maps every nonempty request that returns empty bytes to <code>ERRNO_AGAIN</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi-preview1-component-adapter/src/lib.rs#L2606-L2610\"><code>lib.rs:2606-2610</code></a>). Since no data was returned, <code>fd_read</code> does not advance <code>file.position</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi-preview1-component-adapter/src/lib.rs#L1324-L1329\"><code>lib.rs:1324-1329</code></a>).</p>\n<p>For a regular file, this exposes the initial asynchronous scheduling state as EAGAIN before either file data or a real permission error is available. The same code remains in v50.0.1.</p>\n<h2>Suggested fix and causal evidence</h2>\n<p>For regular files, wait for the initial host read to resolve instead of translating Idle/Waiting empty results directly to EAGAIN. A v46 causal patch used this intervention; the EAGAIN and overwrite disappeared 3/3, returned 3/3 after revert. A complete fix also needs the separate cached-input invalidation described in the stale-read issue when testing a subsequent read.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
